🔥 1. Pod in CrashLoopBackOff
👉 Question:
A pod is continuously restarting. What will you do?
✅ How to Think:
Interviewers expect step-by-step debugging, not guessing.
💡 Strong Answer:
1.	Check pod details:
2.	kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
o	Look for events, errors
3.	Check logs:
4.	kubectl logs <pod-name>
5.	Check previous logs (important):
6.	kubectl logs <pod-name> --previous
7.	Validate:
o	Environment variables
o	ConfigMaps/Secrets
o	Application crash
8.	Check probes:
o	Liveness / Readiness misconfiguration
9.	Resource issues:
o	OOMKilled → increase memory
👉 Bonus (senior-level):
“I also check if recent deployment caused it and consider rollback.”
________________________________________
🔥 2. Application Not Accessible in Browser
👉 Question:
App is deployed but not reachable.
✅ Debug Flow:
•	Pod running?
•	Service created?
•	Ingress configured?
💡 Answer:
1.	Check pods:
2.	kubectl get pods
3.	Check service:
4.	kubectl get svc
5.	Validate:
o	Correct port mapping
o	Service type (ClusterIP / NodePort / LoadBalancer)
6.	If using Ingress:
o	Check ingress rules – (Routing instructions (what to do) eg: define rules - example.com/app1 → goes to app1-service)
o	Check ingress controller – (Traffic manager that applies those instructions (how to do it) eg: NGINX Ingress Controller, AWS ALB Controller)
7.	Network policies (if any)
________________________________________
🔥 3. High Memory Usage in Pods
👉 Question:
Pods are getting killed due to memory.
💡 Answer:
•	Check:
•	kubectl top pod
•	Fix:
o	Increase memory limits
o	Optimize application
o	Set proper requests/limits
👉 Senior Tip:
Use HPA or VPA depending on use case
________________________________________
🔥 4. Rolling Deployment Failure
👉 Question:
New deployment failed. How do you handle?
💡 Answer:
•	Check rollout status:
•	kubectl rollout status deployment <name>
•	Rollback:
•	kubectl rollout undo deployment <name>
•	Identify:
o	Image issue
o	Config issue
👉 Add:
“I ensure readiness probes prevent bad pods from serving traffic.”
________________________________________
🔥 5. Node Not Ready
👉 Question:
Worker node shows NotReady.
💡 Answer:
•	Check node:
•	kubectl describe node <node>
•	Possible causes:
o	Kubelet down
o	Network issue
o	Disk pressure
•	Fix:
o	Restart kubelet
o	Check system logs

