🔥 1. Design a Highly Available Kubernetes Architecture
👉 Question:
Design a highly available Kubernetes cluster for a production system.
💡 What they expect:
You think beyond pods — into control plane + infra
✅ Strong Answer Structure:
Control Plane:
•	Multi-master setup (3 or 5 nodes)
•	etcd cluster (odd number for quorum)
•	API server behind load balancer
Worker Nodes:
•	Spread across multiple AZs
Networking:
•	CNI plugin (Calico / Cilium)
Ingress:
•	ALB / NGINX Ingress Controller
Storage:
•	Persistent volumes (EBS / EFS)
High Availability:
•	Pod Anti-Affinity
•	HPA + Cluster Autoscaler
👉 🔑 Strong line:
“I ensure no single point of failure across control plane, nodes, and networking.”
________________________________________
🔥 2. How Would You Handle Cluster Failure?
👉 Question:
Entire cluster goes down. What’s your recovery plan?
💡 Answer:
Immediate:
•	Check control plane health
•	Restore API access
Recovery:
•	Restore etcd backup
•	Recreate cluster using Terraform
Preventive:
•	Regular etcd backups
•	Multi-region DR strategy
👉 🔑 Add:
“We maintain infra as code to recreate cluster quickly.”
________________________________________
